  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Anticipatory action and response to flood in Adamawa state, NigeriaAnticipatory action and response to flood in Adamawa state, Nigeria</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Nigeria is increasingly vulnerable to climate, hydro-meteorological, hazards such as floods and drought in addition to other crises and socioeconomic challenges. According to the 2025 Seasonal Climate Prediction (SCP), released in February 2025 by the Nigerian Meteorological Agency (NiMet) are expected a late rainy season and strong onset of rainfall in many parts of the country, including flash floods. Through this project, IOM is supporting readiness and response actions that can be triggered right before the crisis hits and at the very onset of the impact. Funding will be used if riverine flooding on Benue River is forecast and the pre-agreed readiness and action trigger thresholds are reached. Upon activation of the action trigger, vulnerable flood-affected people in Adamawa State will receive a well-prioritized package of assistance comprising essentials household items (personal, kitchen, hygiene), tailored shelter solutions with technical assistance, voucher assistance for alternative shelter and house repairs.</narrative>
  </description>
